{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjUwMg==","is_bot":false,"login":"ctate","name":"Chris Tate"},"baseRefOid":"6c7164342a37fab055907f1666658e1333e2cb86","body":"Core path utilities now accept only canonical decimal array indices, preserving numeric-looking tokens as literal object keys and making malformed array reads and writes safe no-ops. Immutable state stores and shared adapters retain snapshot identity for rejected writes, apply valid batch entries progressively, and notify or write only when state changes.\n\nCompound streaming patches validate copy and move sources and destinations, staging moves before mutation so malformed paths cannot insert undefined values or delete their source. Self-referential staged destinations fail closed without aborting stream compilation.\n\nReserved JSON Pointer tokens—__proto__, constructor, and prototype—are rejected before reads, writes, removals, state updates, or compound patch mutation, preventing prototype-chain manipulation. Regression coverage and documentation describe the hardened path and batching contract.","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-14T01:22:49Z","authors":[{"email":"366502+ctate@users.noreply.github.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjUwMg==","login":"ctate","name":"Chris Tate"},{"email":"247288871+simonyang08@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDODr1UJw","login":"simonyang08","name":"SimonYang"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-14T01:22:49Z","messageBody":"Core path utilities now accept only canonical decimal array indices, preserving numeric-looking tokens as literal object keys and making malformed array reads and writes safe no-ops. Immutable state stores and shared adapters retain snapshot identity for rejected writes, apply valid batch entries progressively, and notify or write only when state changes.\n\nCompound streaming patches now validate copy/move sources and destinations, staging moves before mutation so malformed paths cannot insert undefined values or delete their source. Regression coverage and documentation d